ine on node1 (accept_redirects/secure_redirects=1, accept_source_route=0)\",\"Wrote /etc/sysctl.d/60-network-hardening.conf setting net.ipv4.conf.{all,default}.accept_redirects/secure_redirects/accept_source_route = 0\",\"Applied with sysctl --system and verified live values for all/default, but found per-interface (enp1s0, lo) accept_redirects/secure_redirects still 1 due to OR semantics with pre-existing interface state\",\"Extended the config file with explicit net.ipv4.conf.<iface>.* = 0 lines for enp1s0 and lo, re-applied, and verified all live values (all/default/enp1s0/lo) are 0\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id, issued a backgrounded sudo systemctl reboot so the ack returned before disconnection\",\"Polled node1 until exec succeeded again and confirmed a new boot_id (1c9de043... vs baseline d9f8550d...), proving an actual restart\",\"Re-verified post-restart that all/default/enp1s0/lo values for accept_redirects, secure_redirects, and accept_source_route remain 0, and that the persistent config file is intact\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Healthy baseline captured before restart (boot id + current sysctl state)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-e437b86233424e8a\"],\"summary\":\"Captured baseline boot_id d9f8550d... and pre-change sysctl values showing accept_redirects/secure_redirects=1 on node1\"},{\"requirement\":\"Persistently disable ICMP redirect acceptance and source-routed packet acceptance (IPv4)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-0d7f2d707f0a4131\",\"cmd-78cd0714793c4557\"],\"summary\":\"Created /etc/sysctl.d/60-network-hardening.conf, applied via sysctl --system, and after discovering per-interface OR-semantics issue, extended config with explicit enp1s0/lo overrides; verified all/default/enp1s0/lo values are 0 for accept_redirects, secure_redirects, and accept_source_route\"},{\"requirement\":\"Node1 restart acknowledgement returned before disconnection\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-9337bd25b50c4d1e\"],\"summary\":\"Captured pre-restart boot_id and dispatched a backgrounded sudo systemctl reboot; command returned 'reboot command dispatched' before the node disconnected\"},{\"requirement\":\"Poll node1 until command execution available again, proving changed boot identity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-4babb6e834b7425a\",\"cmd-e099f9777eaa41b5\",\"cmd-de6522e88c564527\",\"cmd-923f7dcdb8084873\"],\"summary\":\"Polling attempts failed with connection timeout/reset while node1 was rebooting, then succeeded with a new boot_id 1c9de043-fbc0-444a-b00d-a9e41504fbcd, differing from the baseline d9f8550d..., proving an actual restart occurred\"},{\"requirement\":\"Post-restart recovery of the hardening settings (persistence proof)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-462303be7f434da4\"],\"summary\":\"After reboot, sysctl and /proc/sys checks confirm accept_redirects, secure_redirects, and accept_source_route are still 0 for all/default/enp1s0/lo, and the persisted config file /etc/sysctl.d/60-network-hardening.conf is unchanged and present\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Persistently disabled IPv4 ICMP-redirect acceptance and source-route acceptance on node1 via /etc/sysctl.d/60-network-hardening.conf (covering all, default, and existing interfaces enp1s0/lo), applied live, then restarted node1 and confirmed the settings survived the reboot with a new boot ID.","actions_performed":["Captured pre-change boot_id and sysctl baseline on node1 (accept_redirects/secure_redirects=1, accept_source_route=0)","Wrote /etc/sysctl.d/60-network-hardening.conf setting net.ipv4.conf.{all,default}.accept_redirects/secure_redirects/accept_source_route = 0","Applied with sysctl --system and verified live values for all/default, but found per-interface (enp1s0, lo) accept_redirects/secure_redirects still 1 due to OR semantics with pre-existing interface state","Extended the config file with explicit net.ipv4.conf.<iface>.* = 0 lines for enp1s0 and lo, re-applied, and verified all live values (all/default/enp1s0/lo) are 0","Captured pre-restart boot_id, issued a backgrounded sudo systemctl reboot so the ack returned before disconnection","Polled node1 until exec succeeded again and confirmed a new boot_id (1c9de043... vs baseline d9f8550d...), proving an actual restart","Re-verified post-restart that all/default/enp1s0/lo values for accept_redirects, secure_redirects, and accept_source_route remain 0, and that the persistent config file is intact"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Healthy baseline captured before restart (boot id + current sysctl state)","command_ids":["cmd-e437b86233424e8a"],"summary":"Captured baseline boot_id d9f8550d... and pre-change sysctl values showing accept_redirects/secure_redirects=1 on node1"},{"requirement":"Persistently disable ICMP redirect acceptance and source-routed packet acceptance (IPv4)","command_ids":["cmd-0d7f2d707f0a4131","cmd-78cd0714793c4557"],"summary":"Created /etc/sysctl.d/60-network-hardening.conf, applied via sysctl --system, and after discovering per-interface OR-semantics issue, extended config with explicit enp1s0/lo overrides; verified all/default/enp1s0/lo values are 0 for accept_redirects, secure_redirects, and accept_source_route"},{"requirement":"Node1 restart acknowledgement returned before disconnection","command_ids":["cmd-9337bd25b50c4d1e"],"summary":"Captured pre-restart boot_id and dispatched a backgrounded sudo systemctl reboot; command returned 'reboot command dispatched' before the node disconnected"},{"requirement":"Poll node1 until command execution available again, proving changed boot identity","command_ids":["cmd-4babb6e834b7425a","cmd-e099f9777eaa41b5","cmd-de6522e88c564527","cmd-923f7dcdb8084873"],"summary":"Polling attempts failed with connection timeout/reset while node1 was rebooting, then succeeded with a new boot_id 1c9de043-fbc0-444a-b00d-a9e41504fbcd, differing from the baseline d9f8550d..., proving an actual restart occurred"},{"requirement":"Post-restart recovery of the hardening settings (persistence proof)","command_ids":["cmd-462